  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mekong Inclusive Water Governance and Climate Resilience Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The investment, supported by Mekong-Australia Partnership (MAP) program,  aims to achieve resilient and inclusive development of the Mekong subregion through more inclusive water resource governance and climate resilience in selected riverine communities in Cambodia, Lao PDR, Myanmar, Thailand, and Viet Nam. The investment focuses on elevating the voices of riverine communities, especially women and indigenous people, who are disproportionately affected by large scale infrastructure development and the intensifying climate crisis. The investment builds on  strategic partnerships with  30 local, national, and regional civil society organisations across the Mekong subregion. Through technical, financial and accompaniment support, the investment supports these partners to engage with state actors, the private sector, and inter-governmental bodies at multiple levels to advocate for more inclusive and effective water and climate-related policies, programs, and mechanisms.</narrative>
  </description>
